<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Population risk</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this part we prove the expressions for the Bayes risk and the optimal risk of the attention layer, on population loss, stated in Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Bayes risk and optimality of softmax ‣ 4 Comparison of softmax with alternatives in population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 4.3. ‣ 4.2 Expression of the population risk for arbitrary activation functions ‣ 4 Comparison of softmax with alternatives in population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4.4. ‣ Optimization dynamics and manifold assumption. ‣ 4.2 Expression of the population risk for arbitrary activation functions ‣ 4 Comparison of softmax with alternatives in population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of proposition <a href="#S4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Bayes risk and optimality of softmax ‣ 4 Comparison of softmax with alternatives in population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>: Bayes risk</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the Bayes risk <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Bayes</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume the estimator exactly knows <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Bayes</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not trivially null because the position <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of the relevant token is not known.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The best estimator <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Bayes</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizing the square error on a given sample <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> is the posterior mean of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}=\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|L,k^{*},X)y=\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|L,k^{*},X)\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}X_{\epsilon}^{\top}v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Bayes</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}=\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|L,k^{*},X)y=\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|L,k^{*},X)\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}X_{\epsilon}^{\top}v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The conditional distribution of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> reads</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\epsilon|L,k^{*},X)=P(\epsilon|\chi^{*})=\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi^{*})}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}=1}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi^{*})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\epsilon|L,k^{*},X)=P(\epsilon|\chi^{*})=\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi^{*})}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}=1}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi^{*})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Conditionally on <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{*}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{*}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{*}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xv^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{*}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xv^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be the projections of <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> onto the two relevant directions. They are distributed according to uncorrelated standard Gaussians with law <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We express the empirical means over samples <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> as expectations over one sample. The risk of <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Bayes</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Bayes</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L,k^{*},v^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},X}(y-\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Bayes</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L,k^{*},v^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},X}(y-\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L,k^{*},v^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L\otimes D})}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})(y-\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Bayes</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L,k^{*},v^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L\otimes D})}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})(y-\hat{y}_{\mathrm{Bayes}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=1+\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi^{*},z^{*}}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left[-2z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|\chi^{*})z^{*}_{\epsilon}+\left(\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|\chi^{*})z^{*}_{\epsilon}\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1+\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi^{*},z^{*}}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left[-2z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|\chi^{*})z^{*}_{\epsilon}+\left(\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|\chi^{*})z^{*}_{\epsilon}\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1+\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi^{*}}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left[-2P(\epsilon^{*}|\chi^{*})+\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|\chi^{*})^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1+\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi^{*}}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left[-2P(\epsilon^{*}|\chi^{*})+\sum_{\epsilon}P(\epsilon|\chi^{*})^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi^{*}}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}\frac{g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi)^{2}}{\sum_{\epsilon}g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi^{*}}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}\frac{g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi)^{2}}{\sum_{\epsilon}g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This gives the expression stated in result <a href="#S4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Bayes risk and optimality of softmax ‣ 4 Comparison of softmax with alternatives in population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Risk of the attention layer on population loss</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the risk of the trained attention. We work on population loss. We recall that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> are the weights of the attention. They can be described by the following scalar order parameters (or summary statistics, or sufficient statistics):</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{kk^{*}}=\frac{1}{D}k^{\top}k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{kk^{*}}=\frac{1}{D}k^{\top}k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{vv^{*}}=\frac{1}{D}v^{\top}v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{vv^{*}}=\frac{1}{D}v^{\top}v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{kv^{*}}=\frac{1}{D}k^{\top}v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{kv^{*}}=\frac{1}{D}k^{\top}v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{vk^{*}}=\frac{1}{D}v^{\top}k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{vk^{*}}=\frac{1}{D}v^{\top}k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{kk}=\frac{1}{D}k^{\top}k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{kk}=\frac{1}{D}k^{\top}k</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{vv}=\frac{1}{D}v^{\top}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{vv}=\frac{1}{D}v^{\top}v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{vk}=\frac{1}{D}k^{\top}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{vk}=\frac{1}{D}k^{\top}v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Setting</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\begin{smallmatrix}q_{kk}&amp;q_{vk}\\
q_{vk}&amp;q_{vv}\end{smallmatrix}\right)=\left(\begin{smallmatrix}m_{kk^{*}}\\
m_{vk^{*}}\end{smallmatrix}\right)^{\otimes 2}+\left(\begin{smallmatrix}m_{kv^{*}}\\
m_{vv^{*}}\end{smallmatrix}\right)^{\otimes 2}+\hat{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">q</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">q</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">q</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">q</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\begin{smallmatrix}q_{kk}&amp;q_{vk}\\
q_{vk}&amp;q_{vv}\end{smallmatrix}\right)=\left(\begin{smallmatrix}m_{kk^{*}}\\
m_{vk^{*}}\end{smallmatrix}\right)^{\otimes 2}+\left(\begin{smallmatrix}m_{kv^{*}}\\
m_{vv^{*}}\end{smallmatrix}\right)^{\otimes 2}+\hat{q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}</annotation></semantics></math> a positive <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> matrix, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=m_{kk^{*}}k^{*}+m_{kv^{*}}v^{*}+(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kk}k^{\perp}+(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kv}v^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=m_{kk^{*}}k^{*}+m_{kv^{*}}v^{*}+(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kk}k^{\perp}+(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kv}v^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=m_{vk^{*}}k^{*}+m_{vv^{*}}v^{*}+(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kv}k^{\perp}+(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{vv}v^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=m_{vk^{*}}k^{*}+m_{vv^{*}}v^{*}+(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kv}k^{\perp}+(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{vv}v^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\perp}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\perp}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\perp}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\perp}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> two vectors orthogonal to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and between themselves. We introduce the shorthands</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{kk}=(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{kk}=(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kk}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{kv}=(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{kv}=(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{vv}=(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{vv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{vv}=(\tilde{q}^{1/2})_{vv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kk}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{vv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{vv}</annotation></semantics></math> are related to the magnitude of the components in <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> that are orthogonal to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and bring no information. In the case where there is no overlap between <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and no overlap between <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. when <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=q_{vk}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=q_{vk}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, one can simply express the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>s as <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kk}^{2}=q_{kk}-m_{kk^{*}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kk}^{2}=q_{kk}-m_{kk^{*}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{vv}^{2}=q_{vv}-m_{vv^{*}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{vv}^{2}=q_{vv}-m_{vv^{*}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kv}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kv}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kk}=R_{vv}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kk}=R_{vv}=0</annotation></semantics></math> means that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is perfectly aligned with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The loss depends on <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> only via their projections onto the tokens <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Conditionally on <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce the projections</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\chi^{*}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\chi^{*}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z^{*}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xv^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z^{*}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xv^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xv^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xv^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By central limit theorem we have <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{*}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L}),z^{*}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L}),\xi\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L}),\zeta\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{*}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L}),z^{*}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L}),\xi\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L}),\zeta\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L})</annotation></semantics></math>. For conciseness we introduce the projections of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk=m_{kk^{*}}\chi^{*}+m_{kv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{kk}\xi+R_{kv}\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk=m_{kk^{*}}\chi^{*}+m_{kv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{kk}\xi+R_{kv}\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xv=m_{vk^{*}}\chi^{*}+m_{vv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{kv}\xi+R_{vv}\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xv=m_{vk^{*}}\chi^{*}+m_{vv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{kv}\xi+R_{vv}\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We introduce</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=(m_{kk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},m_{vv^{*}},R_{kk},R_{kv},R_{vv})\in\mathbb{R}^{7}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=(m_{kk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},m_{vv^{*}},R_{kk},R_{kv},R_{vv})\in\mathbb{R}^{7}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">the set of parameters over which the loss is effectively minimized. Then the risk reads</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sigma}(k,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sigma}(k,v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L,k^{*},v^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},X}(y-\hat{y})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L,k^{*},v^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},X}(y-\hat{y})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L,k^{*},v^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L\otimes D}),\epsilon^{*}}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})(y-\hat{y})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L,k^{*},v^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{L\otimes D}),\epsilon^{*}}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})(y-\hat{y})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}-a^{\top}\sigma(b)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}-a^{\top}\sigma(b)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">and the minimal risk is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖤</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{(k,v)\in(\mathbb{R}^{D})^{2}}\mathcal{E}_{\sigma}(k,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{(k,v)\in(\mathbb{R}^{D})^{2}}\mathcal{E}_{\sigma}(k,v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\Theta\in\mathbb{R}^{7}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\Theta\in\mathbb{R}^{7}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Proof of proposition <a href="#S4.Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4.1 Bayes risk and optimality of softmax ‣ 4 Comparison of softmax with alternatives in population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>: the softmax is Bayes-optimal</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recall that the Bayes risk and the optimal risk of the attention estimators are</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Bayes</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi^{*}}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}\frac{g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi)^{2}}{\sum_{\epsilon}g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi^{*}}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon^{*}}\frac{g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi)^{2}}{\sum_{\epsilon}g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖤</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\min_{m_{kk^{*}},m_{vv^{*}}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\left[1-2m_{vv^{*}}g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}+m_{vv^{*}}^{2}g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)^{\top}\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\min_{m_{kk^{*}},m_{vv^{*}}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\left[1-2m_{vv^{*}}g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}+m_{vv^{*}}^{2}g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)^{\top}\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖤</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> we have a upper-bound obtained by restraining the min of eq. (<a href="#A1.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ A.2 Risk of the attention layer on population loss ‣ Appendix A Population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{vk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},R_{vv},R_{kk},R_{kv}=0,0,0,0,0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{vk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},R_{vv},R_{kk},R_{kv}=0,0,0,0,0</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition of the Bayes risk we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}\leq\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Bayes</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝖤</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}\leq\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We search for the optimal <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. We show that it has to match the Bayes-optimal estimator of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. We recall that, from the previous part <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Proof of proposition : Bayes risk ‣ Appendix A Population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, the posterior distribution of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}Xk^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\epsilon|\chi)=\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi)}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}=1}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}\ ." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\epsilon|\chi)=\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi)}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}=1}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">If, for a certain <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{kk^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{kk^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}=P(\epsilon|\chi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}=P(\epsilon|\chi)</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)^{\top}\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)^{\top}\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon}^{L}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}P(\epsilon^{\prime}|\chi)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>χ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon}^{L}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}P(\epsilon^{\prime}|\chi)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon}^{L}\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi)^{2}}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>χ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon}^{L}\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi)^{2}}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">One can notice the similarity with the derivation of the Bayes risk in part <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Proof of proposition : Bayes risk ‣ Appendix A Population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. We proved the equality</p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)^{\top}\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)\ ." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)^{\top}\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">In statistical physics this equality is called the Nishimori condition. It is satisfied when <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> matches the posterior distribution of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimal <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{vv^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{vv^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is then <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{vv^{*}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{vv^{*}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖤</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\chi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon}^{L}\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi)^{2}}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>χ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\chi}\frac{1}{L}\sum_{\epsilon}^{L}\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi)^{2}}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Consequently <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}=\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖤</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Bayes</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}_{\sigma}=\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Bayes}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to show which <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> can satisfy the Nishimori condition. We assume that there is a constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon,\epsilon^{\prime}\in\{1,\ldots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon,\epsilon^{\prime}\in\{1,\ldots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)}{g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}=e^{c_{\nu}(\chi_{\epsilon}-\chi_{\epsilon^{\prime}})}\ ." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{g_{\nu}(\epsilon,\chi)}{g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}=e^{c_{\nu}(\chi_{\epsilon}-\chi_{\epsilon^{\prime}})}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi)_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(\epsilon|\chi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(\epsilon|\chi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi)}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{g(\epsilon,\chi)}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}g(\epsilon^{\prime},\chi)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{e^{c_{\nu}\chi_{\epsilon}}}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}e^{c_{\nu}\chi_{\epsilon^{\prime}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{e^{c_{\nu}\chi_{\epsilon}}}{\sum_{\epsilon^{\prime}}^{L}e^{c_{\nu}\chi_{\epsilon^{\prime}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">that is to say <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is a softmax with inverse temperature <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{kk^{*}}=c_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{kk^{*}}=c_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Invariant manifold</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the main part sec. <a href="#S4" title="4 Comparison of softmax with alternatives in population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> we introduced the manifold</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{(k,v)\in(\mathbb{R}^{D})^{2},m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=q_{vk}=0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{(k,v)\in(\mathbb{R}^{D})^{2},m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=q_{vk}=0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We show that it is invariant by GD. We consider the space of the order parameters, parameterized by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=(m_{vv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},m_{kk^{*}},R_{vv},R_{kk},R_{kv})\in\mathbb{R}^{7}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=(m_{vv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},m_{kk^{*}},R_{vv},R_{kk},R_{kv})\in\mathbb{R}^{7}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We introduce the manifold</p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{M}}=\{\Theta\in\mathbb{R}^{7},m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=R_{kv}=0\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{M}}=\{\Theta\in\mathbb{R}^{7},m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=R_{kv}=0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">At random initialization we have that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=(0,0,0,0,1,0,1)\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=(0,0,0,0,1,0,1)\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider the dynamics given by the gradient flow over the loss <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in eq. (<a href="#A1.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ A.2 Risk of the attention layer on population loss ‣ Appendix A Population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\Theta}=-\nabla_{\Theta}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\Theta}=-\nabla_{\Theta}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We show that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under this dynamics. The gradient in the three directions <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{kv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},R_{kv})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{kv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},R_{kv})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> reads</p>
<table id="A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{m_{kv^{*}}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{m_{kv^{*}}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E64.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}\sigma(b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)a^{\top}\nabla\sigma(b)z^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}\sigma(b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)a^{\top}\nabla\sigma(b)z^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{m_{vk^{*}}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{m_{vk^{*}}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}\sigma(b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)\sigma(b)^{\top}\chi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}\sigma(b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)\sigma(b)^{\top}\chi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{R_{kv}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{R_{kv}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E66.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}\sigma(b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)\left(\sigma(b)^{\top}\xi+a^{\top}\nabla\sigma(b)\zeta\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}\sigma(b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)\left(\sigma(b)^{\top}\xi+a^{\top}\nabla\sigma(b)\zeta\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">At <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=R_{kv}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=R_{kv}=0</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=m_{vv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{vv}\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=m_{vv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{vv}\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=m_{kk^{*}}\chi^{*}+R_{kk}\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=m_{kk^{*}}\chi^{*}+R_{kk}\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, because of the parity with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that the gradient vanishes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.3 </span>Stability of the manifold</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show numerically that the manifold</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{M}}=\{\Theta\in\mathbb{R}^{7},m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=R_{kv}=0\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{M}}=\{\Theta\in\mathbb{R}^{7},m_{kv^{*}}=m_{vk^{*}}=R_{kv}=0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is stable. We simulate the gradient flow</p>
<table id="A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\Theta}=-\nabla_{\Theta}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\Theta}=-\nabla_{\Theta}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">starting from a perturbed random initial condition</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{kk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},m_{vv^{*}},R_{kk},R_{kv},R_{vv})=(0,0,0,0,1,0,1)+\eta\ ," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{kk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},m_{vv^{*}},R_{kk},R_{kv},R_{vv})=(0,0,0,0,1,0,1)+\eta\ ,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\sim\unif([-\bar{\eta},+\bar{\eta}]^{7})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\sim\unif([-\bar{\eta},+\bar{\eta}]^{7})</annotation></semantics></math> some small noise. We consider the value of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> reached after convergence, for several independent realizations of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, for all the configurations considered in the main part of the article. On Figure <a href="#A1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ A.2.3 Stability of the manifold ‣ A.2 Risk of the attention layer on population loss ‣ Appendix A Population risk ‣ Statistical Advantage of Softmax Attention: Insights from Single-Location Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> we observe that all the trajectories converge to a point that belongs to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, up to the numerical errors due to the integration. We additionally observe that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kk}\approx R_{vv}\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kk}\approx R_{vv}\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.21936v1/flotPopBruit.svg" id="A1.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/280;" width="476" height="280"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span> Values of the order parameters <math id="A1.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{kv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},m_{vv^{*}},R_{kk},R_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{kv^{*}},m_{vk^{*}},m_{vv^{*}},R_{kk},R_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{vv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{vv}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained after convergence of the gradient flow. The mean, max and min are taken over the independent runs. The initial noise is <math id="A1.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\eta}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\eta}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and there are at least twenty independent runs.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.4 </span>Orthogonal components on the manifold</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that the minimization of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>, on the previously defined manifold, leads to a vanishing orthogonal component <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{vv}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{vv}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We can show that the second orthogonal component <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kk}</annotation></semantics></math> is null if we assume that the attention is linear.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We recall that on the manifold <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=m_{vv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{vv}\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=m_{vv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{vv}\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=m_{kk^{*}}\chi^{*}+R_{kk}\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=m_{kk^{*}}\chi^{*}+R_{kk}\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. We compute the gradient of the loss with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{vv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{vv}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{R_{vv}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{R_{vv}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}\sigma(b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)\sigma(b)^{\top}\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}\sigma(b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)\sigma(b)^{\top}\zeta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2R_{vv}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},\xi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\sigma(b)^{\top}\sigma(b)}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2R_{vv}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},\xi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\sigma(b)^{\top}\sigma(b)}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where we used the parity with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> and assumed that the supports of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> overlap. As a consequence <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{vv}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{vv}=0</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizer of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We turn to the second orthogonal component <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kk}</annotation></semantics></math>. In full generality <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kk}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kk}=0</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be straightforwardly derived by considering only the gradient <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{R_{kk}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{R_{kk}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> because the gradient may not be monotonous. Instead we assume that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\chi)=1+\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\chi)=1+\chi</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the gradient is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{R_{kk}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{R_{kk}}\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}(1+b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)a^{\top}\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})\left(a^{\top}(1+b)-z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}\right)a^{\top}\xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},\xi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})m_{vv^{*}}^{2}(1+b)^{\top}\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},\xi}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})m_{vv^{*}}^{2}(1+b)^{\top}\xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2R_{kk}m_{vv^{*}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2R_{kk}m_{vv^{*}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and consequently <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{kk}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{kk}=0</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimum of the loss.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.5 </span>Linear attention, stability of the fixed point</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the case of the linear attention <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\chi)=1+\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\chi)=1+\chi</annotation></semantics></math>. For this activation function we can state a more precise result about the stability of the manifold. We show that the fixed point obtained by minimizing the loss on the manifold is stable, i.e. it is a local minimum in the whole space of the order parameters <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{7}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At the fixed point obtained by minimizing the loss on the manifold we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{vk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},R_{vv},R_{kk},R_{kv}=0,0,0,0,0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{vk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},R_{vv},R_{kk},R_{kv}=0,0,0,0,0</annotation></semantics></math>. We compute the Hessian of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{vk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},R_{vv},R_{kk},R_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{vk^{*}},m_{kv^{*}},R_{vv},R_{kk},R_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> at this point. For this we expand <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> to the second order with respect to these five parameters. We have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sigma}=\mathbb{E}_{L}\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*},z^{*},\xi,\zeta}\ g_{\nu}(\epsilon^{*},\chi^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\left(z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}-(m_{vk^{*}}\chi^{*}+m_{vv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{kv}\xi+R_{vv}\zeta)^{\top}\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi^{*}+m_{kv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{kk}\xi+R_{kv}\zeta)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\left(z^{*}_{\epsilon^{*}}-(m_{vk^{*}}\chi^{*}+m_{vv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{kv}\xi+R_{vv}\zeta)^{\top}\sigma(m_{kk^{*}}\chi^{*}+m_{kv^{*}}z^{*}+R_{kk}\xi+R_{kv}\zeta)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
